diff --git a/docs/victoriametrics/vmagent.md b/docs/victoriametrics/vmagent.md
index 87a5b27..db0bdac 100644
--- a/docs/victoriametrics/vmagent.md
+++ b/docs/victoriametrics/vmagent.md
@@ -967,6 +967,27 @@ to all the metrics scraped by the given `vmagent` instance:
 
 See also [how to shard data among multiple remote storage systems](#sharding-among-remote-storages).
 
+## Limiting the number of targets per job
+
+Sometimes a service discovery source (a cloud API, an orchestrator, a catalog, etc.) can misbehave and briefly return
+a much bigger number of targets than expected, for example because of a misconfigured tag filter or an overly broad
+catalog query. Scraping all of them at once may spike CPU and memory usage and degrade scraping for other jobs running
+on the same `vmagent` instance.
+
+To protect against this, the maximum number of active scrape targets a single `job_name` is allowed to have at once
+can be limited via the `max_scrape_targets` option at the corresponding [scrape_config](#how-to-collect-metrics-in-prometheus-format),
+or globally for all jobs via the `-promscrape.maxTargetsPerJob` command-line flag. The `max_scrape_targets` option
+in `scrape_config` overrides the `-promscrape.maxTargetsPerJob` command-line flag for the given job. By default,
+there is no limit on the number of targets per job.
+
+The limit applies uniformly no matter which service discovery mechanism (or combination of mechanisms) produced the
+targets for the given job_name. If the number of discovered targets for a job exceeds the configured limit, then only
+the limit's worth of targets is scraped, while the rest are excluded from scraping and shown as dropped targets with
+the `targets limit` reason at the `http://vmagent:8429/service-discovery` page, and counted at
+`http://vmagent:8429/api/v1/targets`. The `vm_promscrape_scrape_pool_targets{scrape_job="<job_name>", status="dropped_by_limit"}`
+metric exposes the number of targets currently excluded because of the limit for the given job, so alerting rules can
+be set up to notify when a job is being truncated.
+
 ## High availability
 
 It is possible to run multiple **identically configured** `vmagent` instances or `vmagent`
