+    `ScrapeWork` instances rejected for exceeding the limit are registered as dropped targets via
+    the same internal drop-tracking mechanism already used for relabeling/sharding drops (reason
+    "targets limit"), which is why they automatically surface at `WriteServiceDiscovery` and in
+    the dropped-targets list of `WriteAPIV1Targets` without any endpoint-specific code. A
+    per-job `vm_promscrape_scrape_pool_targets{scrape_job=..., status="dropped_by_limit"}` gauge
